<section xml:id="review">
<title>Linear Equations with Vector Coefficients Review</title>
      <exercise>
        <statement>
          <p>
            Consider the following pair of linear equations with vector coefficients:
            <me>x\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\0 \end{pmatrix} + y \begin{pmatrix} 0\\1\end{pmatrix} + z \begin{pmatrix} 1\\1\end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0\\0\end{pmatrix}</me>
            and
            <me>x\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\0 \end{pmatrix} + y \begin{pmatrix} 0\\1\end{pmatrix} + z \begin{pmatrix} 1\\1\end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2\\2\end{pmatrix}.</me>
          </p>
          <ol marker="(a)">
            <li><p>What is a solution to the first equation?</p></li>
            <li><p>What is a solution to the second equation?</p></li>
            <li><p>What happens when we add the two?</p></li>
          </ol>
        </statement>
      </exercise>
    </section>